---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'

const title = 'Features | Klaroly booking app for makeup artists'
const description =
  'Enquiries, a clash-aware calendar, rate cards, digital wedding makeup contracts, invoices, deposits and client notes. See what Klaroly does.'
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description}>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-5 sm:px-8">
    <section class="pt-16 pb-2 sm:pt-24">
      <h1 class="text-4xl leading-[1.1] font-semibold tracking-tight sm:text-5xl">
        What Klaroly does
      </h1>
      <p
        class="mt-6 max-w-xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-[var(--color-muted)] dark:text-[var(--color-muted-dark)]"
      >
        A tour of the parts. Everything here is being built now, and the order is
        being set by the artists we are talking to.
      </p>
    </section>

    <div class="prose max-w-2xl">
      <h2>Enquiries</h2>
      <p>
        Most bookings start as a message you read while your hands are full.
        Klaroly gives enquiries their own place instead of leaving them in an
        inbox.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Add an enquiry in a few taps: name, date, venue, how she found you</li>
        <li>It goes on the calendar as a soft hold straight away</li>
        <li>
          Clash warnings cover enquiries, not just confirmed bookings, so you know
          a date is getting busy before you promise it to somebody
        </li>
        <li>Turn an enquiry into a booking without typing any of it again</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Bookings and the calendar</h2>
      <p>One booking holds the whole job.</p>
      <ul>
        <li>The bride, her contact details, and anybody else involved</li>
        <li>Trial date and wedding date, with times and call times</li>
        <li>The venue, with travel time and distance worked out for you</li>
        <li>What was agreed, what it costs, what has been paid</li>
        <li>List view or calendar view, whichever suits the moment</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Your rate card</h2>
      <p>Set your prices once and stop working them out on a calculator.</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          A line for every service you offer: bride, bridesmaid, mother of the
          bride, children, gents, whatever you call yours
        </li>
        <li>
          Travel, early starts and hotel nights as their own lines, because they
          are their own costs
        </li>
        <li>Override any price on any booking when a job is not standard</li>
        <li>
          Prices are recorded on the booking as they were agreed, so raising your
          rates next year does not quietly rewrite last year
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Contracts</h2>
      <p>The part most artists put off.</p>
      <ul>
        <li>A proper agreement, with your terms and the booking details filled in</li>
        <li>Sent to the bride as a link, nothing for her to download or install</li>
        <li>She reads it, types her full name, ticks the box, submits</li>
        <li>Both of you get a signed PDF immediately</li>
        <li>
          A full record of when it was sent, opened and signed, kept in case it is
          ever needed
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Invoices, deposits and balances</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Deposit on booking, balance before the day, which is how most artists
          already work
        </li>
        <li>Klaroly tracks what is outstanding and how close the date is</li>
        <li>Reminders go out on their own until it is paid, and stop when it is</li>
        <li>
          Record a bank transfer in one tap, because most of your clients will pay
          that way
        </li>
        <li>
          Agreed to wait? Snooze the reminders without pretending the invoice is
          paid
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Client notes and photos</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Notes as a dated stream, so you can see how a booking developed</li>
        <li>Skin type, allergies, sensitivities, the look she wants</li>
        <li>Trial photos and wedding photos at full resolution, kept with the booking</li>
        <li>Add a reminder to any note</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>On your phone, and on your desk</h2>
      <p>
        Klaroly is one product with three faces: an iPhone app, an Android app,
        and a web version for the desktop. The same data in all three.
      </p>
      <p>
        The phone is for the ninety per cent that is tap, tap, done. The desktop
        is for setting up your templates and doing your month end, which nobody
        wants to do with their thumbs.
      </p>

      <h2>What we are deliberately not doing</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Not a directory.</strong> Klaroly does not send you clients and does
          not rank you against other artists. It is your tool, not a marketplace.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Not a form builder.</strong> You will never be asked to design a form.
          Sections turn on and off, that is all.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Not something your clients log into.</strong> Your brides get a link
          when they need one. Nobody is asked to create an account to book a face.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <p><a href="/contact">Join the early access list</a></p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
